Vendored runtime, compositor input and clipboard sources, KRFB patches, and GPU
compatibility sources. Existing source copyright and license notices are retained.
The test-only RFB client in ../../tests/rfb.py is copied from the same source commit.

Local changes:
- The checksum-pinned TigerVNC 1.16.0 viewer forwards actual pointer coordinates
  and buttons on viewport entry. FLTK can deliver the first motion as enter
  after a moved/resized viewer recenters its framebuffer; discarding it leaves
  the remote cursor at a stale position. The patch uses the existing pointer
  handler, without a second motion or coordinate adjustment.
- TigerVNC upstream commits:
  https://github.com/TigerVNC/tigervnc/commit/b7803f74a21bf6a6a7985edd9382d9dda5e7ece4
  https://github.com/TigerVNC/tigervnc/commit/be6e25fca026ce715d5be1d7ba40ef49bebbde51
  These backports preserve the 1.16.0 fingerprint encoding, full digest buffer
  sizes and support Nettle 3 and 4 authentication APIs. All security types remain
  enabled; the displayed RealVNC fingerprint still uses its first eight bytes.
- Native Wayland nesting forwards the position carried by wl_pointer.enter
  before subsequent clicks. A scoped compatibility library preserves all twelve
  current pointer callbacks and the original listener data, including across
  older distro headers and newer compositor SDKs. Its constructor restores the
  application's preload environment; nested init removes conflicting executable
  capabilities for NVIDIA, AMD and software Wayland paths.
- KRFB publishes its actual captured framebuffer size to the input plugin.
  Absolute input is converted from those pixels to the output's logical geometry,
  including its origin, instead of assuming one input pixel per logical unit.
- The test fixture optionally includes the compositor cursor in ScreenShot2
  captures. Tests isolate its full-frame difference against unchanged backgrounds.
- Read-only RFB test clients no longer move the pointer when disconnecting;
  outstanding buttons and keys are still released.
- Docker requests NVIDIA driver injection automatically in every display mode
  and backend when the host driver and NVIDIA runtime exist, preserving explicit
  GPU, runtime, CDI and software-rendering choices.
- Prefer usable NVIDIA EGL devices and pass the selected render node to KWin.
  NVIDIA X11 sessions use a private Xorg virtual screen on a non-default seat,
  without accessing host virtual terminals. Nested X11 sessions present that
  GPU-rendered desktop through an authenticated loopback viewer on the requested
  host transport; Wayland presentation uses its own rootful Xwayland surface and
  an isolated KWin window manager with compositing disabled for older viewers.
- Clipboard relay filters X11 selection negotiation targets (TARGETS, MULTIPLE,
  TIMESTAMP and SAVE_TARGETS) before reading or forwarding data. Their atoms and
  timestamps belong to one X server and are not transferable MIME content.
- X11 kiosk sessions require kwin_x11, without requiring startplasma-x11.
- Kiosk Qt clients use the generic theme, avoiding Qt 6.11's built-in KDE theme
  startup crash when the optional Plasma integration package is absent.
- Restart the compositor after successful exits too: KWin's wrapper returns zero
  when it exhausts its crash retries. Explicit systemd stops still stop it.
- Debian and Ubuntu source variants use the isolated /opt/kwin-6.8.2 stack. Its
  Qt/KF paths and service cache are scoped to KWin and its matching KScreen
  output client; distro applications retain their original library/plugin
  environment. KWin 6.8 changed the output-device registry protocol.
- Allocate and initialize KRFB's virtual-monitor framebuffer before publishing
  its dimensions. An early VNC pixel request otherwise dereferences null before
  PipeWire delivers the first captured frame.
- KRFB requests shared-memory frames for its CPU framebuffer, avoiding oversized
  DMA-BUF modifier lists in KPipeWire's format-negotiation buffer while KWin keeps
  its GPU renderer. Captured images are converted to RGBX8888, matching explicit
  RFB channel shifts 0/8/16 and 255 maxima. Allocate resized buffers before copying
  active pixels row by row, skipping padding. Null images preserve the published
  framebuffer and its geometry.
- Debian KWin 6.3 NVIDIA VNC/web sessions use the software-capture workaround
  only when the optional /opt/kwin-6.8.2 compositor is absent. Source KWin 6.8.2
  retains the normal GPU path in every mode.
- Arch builds the separately namespaced upstream KWin X11 release because its
  current repositories no longer publish kwin-x11.
- Forced Wayland nesting also mounts the host X11 socket when clipboard sync is
  enabled, allowing the Weston clipboard bridge to use its Xwayland fallback.
- The test-only GUI fixture can capture actual headless outputs through KWin's
  ScreenShot2 API or the X11 root screen. Its Save button has a solid color so
  input tests can locate and click the rendered control across nested displays.
- Software Wayland headless sessions on KWin using QPainter reuse the private
  Xvfb backing display for native output capture, with remote servers disabled.
  Test capture errors use stderr directly so Qt logging filters cannot hide them.
- KWin 6.8 software sessions nested on X11 use their virtual compositor and a
  local RFB viewer, avoiding the direct X11 backend's DRI3 requirement. KRFB
  binds only to loopback for this internal relay; viewer clipboard forwarding
  is disabled in favor of the existing text/image relay. Only the source-built
  viewer and libraries missing from the runtime are copied from its build stage.
